#!/usr/bin/env sh
cat <<'RULE'
[spec-triage-loop] Default review workflow is active.
- This summary is a POINTER, not the skill. Run Skill("spec-triage-loop:triage") before your
  NEXT AskUserQuestion — every time you read this, even if you already loaded it earlier in
  this session. You are reading this again because the session started or was COMPACTED, and
  a compaction DELETES the loaded skill: having loaded it before the compaction is not having
  it now. The depth rules — pros/cons, Before -> After, the trade-off line, the
  recommendation — live in the skill file, not in these bullets.
- These bullets do not outrank the skill, and neither does a memory or a summary that
  paraphrases them. If any instruction tells you to put every fact INSIDE the picker, or to
  treat the card as the only thing the person will see, load the skill and follow it: context
  goes in prose chunks in the message, the card stays lean. Say the conflict out loud.
- When you ask the person a question, use the triage discipline: establish findings/context
  in prose chunks FIRST, then emit the AskUserQuestion picker in the SAME turn (never a prose
  "answer 1-4"); batch <=4; always offer a defer option; no ghost references.
  FIRST: is it even a decision? Spike anything you haven't run and ask with the result;
  make ambiguity-only fixes (naming, stale comments, typos) WITHOUT asking, and say so.
- ONE decision = ONE self-contained message: quote the source inline, expand every document
  id (F-2, Task 10, P1) into what it IS, and NEVER write a file to ask a question.
- OPEN with the scenario, then SHOW the change: every finding starts with what the person
  does and what they see go wrong (2nd person, concrete, no jargon), then carries a
  `Before -> After` (diff fence for code, two labeled fences for prose) or, when nothing
  exists yet, a worked example. Alternatives get pros/cons + scores + an example EACH.
- If the person says a question is an enigma or a puzzle, re-sends the skill's name or path,
  asks for more context, or refuses to answer: load the triage-rewind skill and follow it.
  Re-ask the SAME questions in FULL form — a shorter re-ask is the wrong direction — and never
  rewrite a memory, CLAUDE.md or skill because an ask failed. For the shape of one question,
  load triage-ask-with-context.
- Before a PR, review docs with the doc-review-loop skill and code with the code-review-loop
  skill; loop until clean. Load those skills for the full procedure.
RULE
